<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11578" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crētātus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>marked with chalk</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fasciae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 2, 3, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pedes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 18, 58, § 201</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bos (decorated as an offering),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					10, 66</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fabulla,</span>”
				<i>whitened</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 2, 41, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: ambitio, i. e. <i>of
				the candidates for office, clothed in white</i> (candidatorum),
				<i><span class="en">Pers.
				5, 177</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
